and media change", "children": [{"id": "b54ee792-fcf9-4759-956d-3efd4f63ee6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Cold War and postcolonial contexts"}, {"id": "2a9cf2f8-b446-49b2-9699-7bde921b72da", "type": "concept", "title": "Mass media and spectatorship"}, {"id": "083c3ea4-ee9e-4fa7-978b-fc622df732b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Technology as historical force"}], "description": "Students connect cinema to postwar politics, decolonization, television, video, digital media, and globalization."}]}, {"id": "561cd292-ca4f-4a91-a561-1291105f065a", "type": "topic", "title": "Postwar Film Culture and International Art Cinema", "description": "This section shows how postwar festivals, critics, art houses, auteurs, and cinephile institutions created a new international film culture.", "children": [{"id": "e9f825d9-30cf-486e-a55f-eafe54dbdd8a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Festival and art-house systems", "children": [{"id": "89732ba0-ee49-4e1d-b89c-5ed4336f9a69", "type": "concept", "title": "Cannes, Venice, Berlin, and festival prestige"}, {"id": "85b7fe65-8c8b-4434-9dfe-b460b7667c84", "type": "concept", "title": "Art-house distribution and subtitled cinema"}, {"id": "8b54b7d7-b8d6-4d56-91f7-e9434f12e386", "type": "concept", "title": "Cine-clubs, critics, and film journals"}], "description": "Students learn how exhibition institutions shaped what counted as serious cinema."}, {"id": "f6e32818-29fe-4e9c-ad39-bb19f40a03c3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Auteurs and modernist narration", "children": [{"id": "9271812b-4f85-499a-9f8f-19678669258c", "type": "concept", "title": "Authorial signature"}, {"id": "eec7b0dc-c603-4cda-a45c-454bb28b8304", "type": "concept", "title": "Psychological ambiguity"}, {"id": "040b1e7c-1db9-4400-9f3f-74e29e1f35b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Ellipsis, reflexivity, and open form"}], "description": "The gist is to study ambiguity, style, subjectivity, and open endings as historical art-cinema conventions."}, {"id": "302cb0f4-55f1-4210-8be0-b64bd5042