evolution, poverty, memory, and popular culture."}, {"id": "09a2da7c-a4f0-4e1a-af9e-ceecdfb364cc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Middle Eastern and Iranian cinemas", "children": [{"id": "632115e1-8b30-4937-ac83-1d5a07bc0a69", "type": "concept", "title": "Iranian art cinema"}, {"id": "e2a232ee-8ce8-4b6e-aa1d-1ae2eb0b89af", "type": "concept", "title": "Palestinian and diasporic cinema"}, {"id": "65cb4466-6733-4ba3-87c4-9bfaf2dd5529", "type": "concept", "title": "Egyptian popular cinema and regional industries"}], "description": "Students study censorship, allegory, realism, gender, religion, and transnational reception."}]}, {"id": "c6c26a69-e8f0-460b-9443-c88e771f1b0a", "type": "topic", "title": "Documentary Movements", "description": "This section examines documentary after World War II as a field of technology, ethics, observation, activism, television, and political memory.", "children": [{"id": "908c3a9a-3bc9-4e11-9dcb-8f519b8116a8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Direct cinema and cinema verite", "children": [{"id": "f7263036-493f-4935-a2fc-9cb21f374abe", "type": "concept", "title": "Observation, performance, and presence"}, {"id": "9bb23475-96f9-433d-b710-9eb803bb9012", "type": "concept", "title": "Filmmaker intervention versus invisibility"}, {"id": "5431ec0f-9294-4db6-9260-e236cf0ff151", "type": "concept", "title": "Truth claims and editing"}], "description": "Students learn how lightweight cameras and sync sound changed nonfiction practice."}, {"id": "1f353b8b-2c25-4928-9ac0-65954b1df73f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Political and essay documentary", "children": [{"id": "dbb90dc7-8371-44d9-ac25-cc16a875a87a", "type": "concept", "title": "Third Cinema and activist documentary"}, {"id": "e7385c1b-5ede-472e-b957-7e1d11eea579", "type": "concept", "title": "Essay film and first-person narration"}, {"id": "be8dee94-d616-4e83-aa6a-94e1b0587dd3", "type": "concept", "title": "Archives, memory, and trauma"}], "description": "The gist is to study documentary as argument, testimony, and historical intervention."}, {"id": "6d42a508-159f-44e2-8ad7-8ce50563ca74", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contemporary nonfiction ecosystems", "children": [{"id": "d87cf815-44a3-46b2-83ce-f770f97eece3", "type": "concept", "title": "Docuseries and platform formats"}, {"id": "2e756023-f069-4595-a3b5-49ce17d61be0", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethics of representation and consent"}, {"id": "c566e054-64eb-495b-a578-b126f32ffc55", "type": "concept", "title": "Impact producing and public debate"}], "description": "Students connect documentary to television, festivals, streaming, true crime, and impact campaigns."}]}, {"id": "abf64ff0-9080-4d9a-84c7-a4aeecb3e1cb", "type": "topic", "title": "Experimental, Avant-Garde, and Essay Film", "description": "Experimental cinema challenges narrative, spectatorship, medium boundaries, and institutional definitions of film.", "children": [{"id": "e9201870-221a-4ad9-92f7-0f3d3d642af8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Postwar avant-garde traditions", "children": [{"id": "29b9c934-3522-49b1-b42a-0ec789020ece", "type": "concept", "title": "Structural film"}, {"id": "0f4b2afe-a249-4a18-b056-388de0ba71d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Expanded cinema"}, {"id": "82540f6e-338e-4eeb-af20-cc7641755693", "type": "concept", "title": "Found footage and material film"}], "description": "Students learn how experimental filmmakers explored perception, materiality, duration, and embodiment."}, {"id": "f5acd7b9-38ca-4d59-9df9-4443d8cca1eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Video and time-based art", "children": [{"id": "37b78069-02c5-4168-86b0-afb7d89810e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Portapak and early video art"}, {"id": "f88f69a8-4c49-4d8e-95b5-4391e1728f65", "type": "concept", "title": "Projection, monitors, and installation contexts"}, {"id": "5270959d-23d4-45b2-b797-a2984559ecbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Performance and documentation"}], "description": "The point is to connect film history with gallery, performance, installation, and electronic media."}, {"id": "109e95c2-e9b9-4261-8b8e-c2db222d040c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Essay film and hybrid forms", "children": [{"id": "b0749a4c-1b75-4586-8db1-f98b0725202b", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice, text, and image thinking"}, {"id": "f016b2e6-9646-4459-8bba-f50419246b06", "type": "concept", "title": "Personal and political memory"}, {"id": "9555619c-d3fd-41ff-b10a-d27e7993ec36", "type": "concept", "title": "Hybrid documentary-fiction structures"}], "description": "Students study works that combine argument, memory, archive, travel, and self-reflection."}]}, {"id": "828e85ba-761e-4697-a83d-4e12150a800b", "type": "topic", "title": "Feminist, Queer, Black, Indigenous, and Decolonial Film Histories", "description": "This section centers counter-histories, not as add-ons, but as necessary frameworks for understanding modern cinema.", "children": [{"id": "d3928cf5-47b4-4b08-9686-de9514bfac53", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Feminist film histories", "children": [{"id": "b469c972-e33d-462a-a7f7-2620b8962c9f", "type": "concept", "title": "Second-wave feminist film culture"}, {"id": "6a13c5f9-a88c-4f16-86f8-50c6a90bac1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Women directors, editors, writers, and producers"}, {"id": "fc57d9ec-e38e-49b0-80f6-b58a1196dec6", "type": "concept", "title": "The gaze, spectatorship, and critique"}], "description": "Students study women filmmakers, feminist criticism, labor, spectatorship, and representation."}, {"id": "8cc752a0-5875-4cd1-8713-b105c03e3d64", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Queer and Black film histories", "children": [{"id": "47149b49-51a8-46ec-9913-891a375dce85", "type": "concept", "title": "New Queer Cinema"}, {"id": "1d3467cb-6630-4ba2-b69b-1a81f941b0f5", "type": "concept", "title": "L.A. Rebellion and Black independent cinema"}, {"id": "d1abff14-d4a2-4b81-baa3-b96d472b488e", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation, authorship, and audience publics"}], "description": "The gist is to trace identity, form, community, market, and resistance."}, {"id": "09f4b8d0-0f77-45cd-81e3-9f2a966cce2c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Indigenous and decolonial cinemas", "children": [{"id": "cce4ee94-cb00-4106-986e-1833c7183100", "type": "concept", "title": "Fourth Cinema and Indigenous media"}, {"id": "b80bc52e-bff2-436b-98db-f64547eaa2dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Decolonial documentary and fiction"}, {"id": "7bfe2a1e-6af0-445c-b2ca-ae456d241536", "type": "concept", "title": "Community accountability and cultural protocols"}], "description": "Students examine sovereignty, land, language, memory, and anti-colonial image-making."}]}, {"id": "33699744-184f-4d40-a439-06afb40b190c", "type": "topic", "title": "Television, Video, and Media Convergence", "description": "Film history after 1960 cannot be separated from television, home video, music video, cable, games, and digital convergence.", "children": [{"id": "47c7dd4d-3046-4f4b-bc73-2fd37af35c00", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Television and film culture", "children": [{"id": "323dc9b8-c4c6-4fe0-ac75-d28829952525", "type": "concept", "title": "Broadcast competition and made-for-TV movies"}, {"id": "cd604aba-33c5-46ba-a66f-ebbd5d4dc567", "type": "concept", "title": "Cable, HBO, and prestige television"}, {"id": "1dcec09d-4d57-49bc-9958-5a8c31e9391c", "type": "concept", "title": "Seriality and long-form storytelling"}], "description": "Students learn how television changed audiences, financing, aesthetics, and prestige."}, {"id": "6af09939-4244-4248-980a-224705256e5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Home video and cinephilia", "children": [{"id": "751e460e-54a3-4a80-8621-a959cf9809dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Rental culture and video stores"}, {"id": "a5babc57-14fe-47d0-aa34-56fde0fc29a2", "type": "concept", "title": "DVD extras and cinephile education"}, {"id": "5be88a48-08e2-41ae-9047-4f195106d01d", "type": "concept", "title": "Cult film and midnight movie circulation"}], "description": "The point is to understand VHS, DVD, and boutique labels as historical forces."}, {"id": "014e2381-103e-4b99-a2e6-c2ceb26c32fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Convergence and transmedia", "children": [{"id": "fa83242d-77f7-4a9d-a10f-1d4407b6b99c", "type": "concept", "title": "Music video and advertising aesthetics"}, {"id": "bcd06a3a-e528-4c7a-be2a-351337d0c37f", "type": "concept", "title": "Games, comics, and franchise worlds"}, {"id": "8ac57ef8-946b-45cc-bb79-5da5dbbfcc68", "type": "concept", "title": "Participatory fandom and online communities"}], "description": "Students connect film to wider media systems."}]}, {"id": "b4c3b509-c9c0-4bc7-8bb1-cc8ac0523a8f", "type": "topic", "title": "The Digital Cinema Revolution", "description": "Digital technologies changed production, post-production, distribution, exhibition, preservation, and the look of moving images.", "children": [{"id": "a26947ff-ee21-47da-8d08-66815172268e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital production and post-production", "children": [{"id": "93a6b3fd-0a93-4963-88d9-5146da3b8808", "type": "concept", "title": "DV, HD, and digital cinematography"}, {"id": "2acee5e9-adbe-4b82-a742-097f84be738b", "type": "concept", "title": "Nonlinear editing and compositing"}, {"id": "8734c43f-24bc-40df-981c-49d8a76421fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital color grading and DI workflows"}], "description": "Students learn how digital cameras, editing systems, VFX, and color workflows changed filmmaking."}, {"id": "4429517e-ae36-4bcb-9fc6-39aae9730f8d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital aesthetics", "children": [{"id": "3dd9f01b-b569-45a5-aab6-6f66755e454b", "type": "concept", "title": "CGI and photorealism"}, {"id": "5c4f3091-9174-401c-ab4a-8af2f54a943c", "type": "concept", "title": "Motion capture and virtual production"}, {"id": "6b3b44d5-f658-4a59-b4d4-caf5f8222013", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-budget digital realism"}], "description": "The gist is to study how digital tools changed realism, spectacle, movement, and time."}, {"id": "0fcff154-8226-4814-9d54-f42eb45cdb0f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Distribution and exhibition change", "children": [{"id": "0c877e00-6685-42a6-83a2-7bc094ae66bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital projection"}, {"id": "59679fdc-331f-4e8f-8f01-5398b45df31a", "type": "concept", "title": "Online circulation and piracy"}, {"id": "120463f4-1541-4482-9227-e87d29ecad08", "type": "concept", "title": "DCP, restoration, and preservation challenges"}], "description": "Students connect digital cinema to theaters, festivals, piracy, and global access."}]}, {"id": "7d1390bf-a275-40a4-82a8-d6995118931c", "type": "topic", "title": "Contemporary Global Cinema", "description": "This section treats contemporary cinema as a network of national industries, festivals, platforms, diasporas, auteurs, genres, and uneven power.", "children": [{"id": "53685ccb-51ca-45e5-9579-a58eee2e3c1a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global auteurs and festival cinema", "children": [{"id": "589cdad2-c1e9-4ecd-867b-5775140c696e", "type": "concept", "title": "Festival discovery and awards economies"}, {"id": "26b56da4-8dbc-4a87-a4be-9da0e15983d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Slow cinema and contemplative style"}, {"id": "b944ef6a-7aac-4407-b81a-6f33522c2e4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Global art-house branding"}], "description": "Students learn how contemporary prestige cinema is produced, circulated, and valued."}, {"id": "296ece35-d3f6-4982-aa39-dbb1a008b862", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Popular global industries", "children": [{"id": "1b74dcab-7761-44be-ae0e-202a5792b61a", "type": "concept", "title": "Bollywood, Nollywood, Korean cinema, and Chinese markets"}, {"id": "2c805d0f-5db7-441a-b33a-25b104f45d13", "type": "concept", "title": "Regional genres and stars"}, {"id": "ed88bf32-e8f3-4b0f-876e-c2bd8f50ed7b", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-border remakes and co-productions"}], "description": "The point is to study popular film industries with their own histories and logics."}, {"id": "f71c2ee8-