3f-4fd6-bf03-1a3ed7af55b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Labor, access, and cultural memory", "children": [{"id": "ce62c869-dfd4-41ed-a1d0-317b7e33649e", "type": "concept", "title": "Residuals, strikes, and creative labor"}, {"id": "4c7bb4b1-bb97-4a7f-a09b-5a161492c3de", "type": "concept", "title": "Catalog instability and disappearance"}, {"id": "e309c2b1-56c3-42f1-838c-5d35be24a404", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility, subtitling, dubbing, and global publics"}], "description": "Students evaluate the consequences of digital abundance and platform control."}]}, {"id": "21637c7d-a5f5-4844-933c-7be4eb447d44", "type": "topic", "title": "Archives, Restoration, and Canon Formation in the Modern Era", "description": "Modern film history depends on what is preserved, restored, subtitled, programmed, streamed, taught, and made available.", "children": [{"id": "2b029995-7851-4d57-9aa0-c4b38298ee4d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Restoration and preservation", "children": [{"id": "074efeff-b63e-43fc-b57a-24aab1e46174", "type": "concept", "title": "Analog-to-digital restoration"}, {"id": "6d2be596-c2d7-4f4d-bbb4-830494ea117e", "type": "concept", "title": "Born-digital fragility"}, {"id": "a7e1ac49-00d2-41d2-8013-34db9b35f87c", "type": "concept", "title": "Color, sound, aspect ratio, and version choices"}], "description": "Students learn how modern and digital cinema create new preservation challenges."}, {"id": "aa52e453-9c35-4c1f-b30e-3a2d2a9eb067", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Archives and curatorial power", "children": [{"id": "f2d519c7-d317-47cd-aeda-0fe79610f7de", "type": "concept", "title": "National archives, university archives, and private collections"}, {"id": "687a79fc-4d0b-444b-9427-4a85a2ff84ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Criterion, BFI, UCLA, LOC, and boutique distribution"}, {"id": "3e3aa7aa-d920-4f44-99f1-eb84507d605a", "type": "concept", "title": "Rights, access, and programming"}], "description": "The point is to understand institutions as active makers of film history."}, {"id": "d59d031b-c0ab-4644-b74e-399bc0c69659", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Canon revision", "children": [{"id": "34b8e5ae-25eb-4946-aef1-ae7a35166608", "type": "concept", "title": "Women, Black, queer, Indigenous, and global canons"}, {"id": "899ca959-617a-48e9-857c-3142ba107e1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Festival and critic poll influence"}, {"id": "cc7c6a33-c931-4c09-a2a9-a08a5cd3336c", "type": "concept", "title": "Pedagogical selection and historical responsibility"}], "description": "Students practice questioning inherited lists and syllabi."}]}, {"id": "b5f4b11b-534a-4fbd-8cac-5dc5bb432ea4", "type": "topic", "title": "Modern Film-History Research Capstone", "description": "The capstone asks students to produce a historically grounded argument about modern or contemporary cinema using film analysis, sources, and context.", "children": [{"id": "e97d3326-237a-4fdc-91bc-94a1f5907e33", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research design", "children": [{"id": "16723452-8502-4fd4-864e-d8e17bc7ee62", "type": "concept", "title": "Topic scope and case selection"}, {"id": "d4defbc7-e35a-4c57-9109-e84b2892b3c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Annotated bibliography and source map"}, {"id": "63212958-6e66-49d1-8057-5be809e8092d", "type": "concept", "title": "Historical stakes and research contribution"}], "description": "Students develop a focused question that can be answered with films, scholarship, criticism, archives, and industry evidence."}, {"id": "b00ba3f2-6212-4017-97f0-0af74f811e2f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence and analysis", "children": [{"id": "10c3d70e-2dea-4f3c-8345-5903c6ac398d", "type": "concept", "title": "Sequence analysis"}, {"id": "22ec39de-2f2d-4b1c-89eb-4187afd1b588", "type": "concept", "title": "Reception and industry evidence"}, {"id": "105c467a-2a94-41d4-a3f6-255041f4fd7c", "type": "concept", "title": "Comparative or transnational framing"}], "description": "The focus is on connecting film form to history rather than summarizing plots or movements."}, {"id": "7c6b0349-a9a0-421b-9ffc-630d2d20ede9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Final paper and presentation", "children": [{"id": "bfe490b2-2ced-42cd-a656-eba5ae24d014", "type": "concept", "title": "Clip or still-based oral presentation"}, {"id": "041f08aa-c9ca-4892-916c-2ebc2dfcf512", "type": "concept", "title": "Research paper with revision"}, {"id": "52960871-28e7-43b1-830b-2cbb4cc9b4a4", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflection on archive, canon, and method"}], "description": "Students communicate a polished argument for a film-studies audience."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$fh2json$::jsonb,
